      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Meet the founder",
        "name": "Tianna McFarlane",
        "title": "Award-winning entrepreneur · Founder & CEO",
        "biography": "<p>Tianna McFarlane is an award-winning entrepreneur and the founder of Heal In Colour, Canada’s first inclusive bandage brand.</p><p>The idea started with a simple moment. Tianna cut her knee, went looking for a bandage that matched her skin, and couldn’t find one. So she built the solution herself. She launched Heal In Colour in April 2021, and it’s now sold in Loblaws stores across Canada and used by school boards, universities and workplaces nationwide.</p><p>In a rare honour, Heal In Colour’s prototypes and products were preserved by <a href=\"https://collection.ingenium.ca/en/search/?q=heal+in+colour&type=all&sort=score_des&page=1\" title=\"https://collection.ingenium.ca/en/search/?q=heal+in+colour&type=all&sort=score_des&page=1\">Ingenium, Canada’s National Science and Technology collection centre</a>, for their significance to Canadian history.</p><p>Tianna’s work has earned national recognition. She is the 2026 recipient of the George Weston Entrepreneurship Award, presented by the BlackNorth Initiative, and has been named a Toronto Star Changemaker.&nbsp;</p><p>Tianna’s message is simple: representation belongs everywhere, even in the first aid kit.</p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/whoweare_img_c0494849-3ccb-4641-bb27-dc2ca2975914.png",
